EFE and reward-only Planning are not significantly different on reward ($-21.53$ vs.\ $-21.39$, seed-level Welch $p{=}0.82$) or success (72.0\% vs.\ 73.8\%, $p{=}0.17$), failures to reject rather than a TOST-backed equivalence claim as in Section~\ref{sec:sarsop}, but EFE uses significantly fewer scans (14.75 vs.\ 15.64, seed-level $p{=}8.8{\times}10^{-5}$, pooled $p<10^{-13}$). Planning+IG's 32.25 scans, more than double EFE's, erode reward despite 97.3\% success, the over-exploration pattern of Diagnosis and Bandit at a larger scale. Figure~\ref{fig:tw_comparison} shows the mechanism. EFE concentrates belief by partition-based narrowing and commits once confident, Planning lacks scan-selection guidance, and InfoGain-Tuned keeps scanning past the point of diminishing returns. InfoGain-Tuned, the figure's bottom row, is the myopic Info Gain agent of Table~\ref{tab:agents} at its own success-tuned weight, a different agent from the tree-search Planning+IG row of Table~\ref{tab:tileworld}, which adds the same bonus at every node of its lookahead tree.

